WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
999: an emergency, danger to life. You can also go to A&E (the hospital emergency department). 111: urgent but not an emergency. It is free and you can also use 111.nhs.uk. For minor problems, go to the pharmacy first.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
In England, with «Pharmacy First», the pharmacy can treat you without a GP appointment for 7 conditions: sore throat, ear infection, impetigo, shingles, infected insect bites, sinusitis and uncomplicated urinary tract infections in women (there are age limits).

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:45.300
Prescriptions are charged only in England (£9.90 per item in 2025/26; check the current price). Some people are exempt. The Immigration Health Surcharge does not cover prescriptions or the dentist.

4
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:52.500
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
